#question(title: [Derivatives of
$display((f circle.small g))$], centered: true)[
  Assume $f$ and $g$ are functions that have
  all their derivatives. Find formulas for
  + $display((f circle.small g)' (x))$
  + $display((f circle.small g)^(' ') (x))$
  + $display((f circle.small g)^(' ' ') (x))$

  in terms of the values of $f$, $g$ and
  their derivatives.

  #emph[Hint:] The first one is simply the
  chain rule.

  #emph[Challenge:] Find a formula for
  $display((f circle.small g)^((n)) (x))$
   \
  (This is beyond the scope of this course).
]
